w: 1.~Am I a sol- dier of the cross, A fol- lower of the Lamb, _ And shall I fear to own His cause, Or blush to speak His name?
w: 2.~Must I be car- ried to the skies On flow- ery beds of ease, _ While o- thers fought to win the prize, And sailed through blood- y seas?
w: 3.~Are there no foes for me to face? Must I not stem the flood? _ Is this vile world a friend to grace, To help me on to God?
w: 4.~Sure I must fight if I would reign; In- crease my cou- rage, Lord. _ I’ll bear the toil, en- dure the pain, Sup- por- ted by Thy Word.
w: 5.~Thy saints in all this glor- ious war Shall con- quer, though they die; _ They see the tri- umph from a- far, By faith’s di- scer- ning eye.
w: 6.~When that il- lus- trious day shall rise, And all Thy arm- ies shine _ In robes of vic- tory through the skies, The glo- ry shall be Thine.
